REGEDIT4

; Where the .NET Framework is, as Windows' own mscoree.dll registers it: the
; Framework's installer, made for Windows 8 and later, takes that part as the
; system's and leaves it out. Arctic's mscoree (Wine patch 0156) finds
; mscoreei.dll of the Framework here (docs/dotnet.md).

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\Microsoft\.NETFramework]
"InstallRoot"="C:\\Windows\\Microsoft.NET\\Framework64\\"

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\Wow6432Node\Microsoft\.NETFramework]
"InstallRoot"="C:\\Windows\\Microsoft.NET\\Framework\\"
